# Test Architecture (BDD + Playwright)

## Goal

Make tests:

- readable as specification (Gherkin)
- resistant to flakes (condition-first waits)
- cheap to maintain (thin steps)
- convenient for AI agents (explicit selectors/waits/context)

## Layering

| Layer | Responsibility | Must NOT contain |
|------|----------------|------------------|
| `.feature` | WHAT: business intent + explicit expectations | hidden branching, implementation details |
| Step Definitions | HOW (wiring): call the right API/fixture | loops, retries, complex if/else |
| Fixtures/Utils | HOW (mechanics): Playwright interactions, waits | business rules, scenario asserts |
| Page Objects / Components | UI surface: locators + small actions | end-to-end flows, environment setup |

## Suggested structure

```
features/
  smoke/
  regression/
support/
  step_definitions/
  fixtures/
  pages/
  utils/
```

## Conventions

- One step = one action (click/fill/assert).
- All asserts — only in `Then`.
- No `sleep` without condition.
- Locators: `data-testid` → role/name → label/placeholder → text (last resort).

